{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.BorelWatsonShiftFull","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mathlib.BorelWatsonShiftFull","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.BorelWatsonUniqueness","lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.BorelWatsonBoundary","lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.BorelWatsonShift"],"declarations":5,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Borel.watson_uniqueness_rhp_open","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Borel.watson_uniqueness_rhp_open","kind":"theorem","line":151,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/BorelWatsonShiftFull.lean#L151-L174","doc":"**Watson uniqueness on the open right half-plane — COMPLETE.** The capstone:\nif the shifted Watson hypotheses hold on every strictly-interior half-plane\n`{re > ε}` (ε > 0), then `f = g` on the whole open half-plane `{re > 0}`.\nComposes `watson_uniqueness_shifted` (each `{re ≥ ε}` instance) with the\nε-reduction `eqOn_rhp_of_eqOn_shifted` (brick 4b-ii boundary), which lets\n`ε → 0` while never touching the boundary puncture at `0`. This closes the\nWatson / Nevanlinna–Sokal uniqueness gap on the half-plane. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Borel.watson_uniqueness_shifted","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Borel.watson_uniqueness_shifted","kind":"theorem","line":118,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/BorelWatsonShiftFull.lean#L118-L149","doc":"**Shifted Watson uniqueness.** Brick 3's `watson_uniqueness_rhp`, transported\nto the shifted half-plane `{re ≥ ε}` by applying it to `w ↦ f(w+ε)`,\n`w ↦ g(w+ε)` on `{re > 0}`. All six hypotheses move across the shift: the\n`DiffContOnCl` regularity via `diffContOnCl_comp_add_const`, the growth\nbounds via `isBigO_exp_shift`, and (directly, matching the shifted\nevaluation points) the imaginary-axis→vertical-line `{re = ε}` boundedness\nand the shifted positive-real-axis stretched-exp decay. The conclusion is\npulled back from `{re ≥ 0}` to `{re ≥ ε}` by `w = z − ε`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Borel.isBigO_exp_shift","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Borel.isBigO_exp_shift","kind":"theorem","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/BorelWatsonShiftFull.lean#L60-L116","doc":"**Growth-bound transport.** The brick-3 growth hypothesis\n`∃ c < 2, ∃ B, f =O exp(B‖z‖^c)` on `{re > ε}` moves to the same shape for\n`w ↦ f(w+ε)` on `{re > 0}`. After `comp_tendsto` (giving\n`f' =O exp(B‖w+ε‖^c)`), the exponent/coefficient are normalized to\n`c' = max c 0 ∈ [0,2)`, `B' = max B 0 · 2^{c'}`, using `‖w+ε‖ ≤ 2‖w‖` and\nrpow monotonicity — all valid eventually since `‖w‖ → ∞` on `cobounded`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Borel.tendsto_addRight_shifted","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Borel.tendsto_addRight_shifted","kind":"theorem","line":47,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/BorelWatsonShiftFull.lean#L47-L58","doc":"The filter of brick 3's growth hypothesis, `cobounded ⊓ 𝓟 {re > 0}`, is\ncarried by `w ↦ w + ε` to `cobounded ⊓ 𝓟 {re > ε}`: coboundedness is\npreserved and the open half-plane `{re > 0}` maps into `{re > ε}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Borel.tendsto_addRight_cobounded","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Borel.tendsto_addRight_cobounded","kind":"theorem","line":36,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/BorelWatsonShiftFull.lean#L36-L45","doc":"Translation `w ↦ w + ε` preserves coboundedness: `Tendsto (·+ε) cobounded\ncobounded`. Via `‖w + ε‖ ≥ ‖w‖ − ‖ε‖ → ∞` on `cobounded`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}